{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/math\/workingwithquantity"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/WorkingWithQuantity","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Math"}],"title":"Working with Quantity","roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/StoringAndEncodingQuantities","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/UnitsByDimension","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Create, convert, compare, compute with, and format ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity"},{"text":" values in your app.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the type you’ll reach for most often. It works the way"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Foundation’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Measurement"},{"type":"text","text":" does, but with compile-time dimension checking: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"quantity always knows its unit, and its unit knows its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This article covers everything you can do with a quantity, grouped the same way"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Apple documents its own value types."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Create a Quantity","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Create-a-Quantity"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a quantity with a value and a unit using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/init(value:unit:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Math","","\/\/ Distance","let jumpLength = Quantity(value: 8.95, unit: Units.meter)","","\/\/ Money — currency units place their symbol before the value ($8.95)","let price = Quantity(value: 8.95, unit: Units.usd)","","\/\/ Temperature — offset units like Celsius convert correctly","let bodyTemp = Quantity(value: 37.0, unit: Units.celsius)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The value is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":", so you can pass integer literals directly:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Quantity(value: 42, unit: Units.kilometer)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"text":"Convert Between Units","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Convert-Between-Units"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/converted(to:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to convert to another unit of the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension. The framework converts through the unit’s base unit, so arbitrary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chains like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nanometer → kilometer"},{"type":"text","text":" just work:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let chipFeature = Quantity(value: 5.0, unit: Units.nanometer)","let inMeters = chipFeature.converted(to: Units.meter)","print(inMeters.value) \/\/ 